From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:05:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] react: expose local query-result removal

Expose a non-throwing local-result presence check and a one-shot removal observer on Watch. Applications can now wait for a removed subscription's retained success or error to leave the local sync state without reaching into ConvexReactClient internals or creating another subscription.

Keep the initial presence check and transition-handler registration synchronous and attached to the same sync generation, and cover the complete Add, QueryUpdated, Remove, and QueryRemoved lifecycle with an in-memory WebSocket test.
---
 src/browser/sync/client.test.ts | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/react/client.ts             | 51 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

